## Quick Reference: Lesson 007

### Variable Definition

```asm
LabelName:  EQU $address    ; Define variable at address
```

### Store to Memory

```asm
LD A,value          ; Load value into A
LD (address),A      ; Store A to memory
LD (label),A        ; Store A using label
```

### Load from Memory

```asm
LD A,(address)      ; Load from memory into A
LD A,(label)        ; Load using label
```

### Direction Encoding

| Value | Direction | Visual Indicator |
|-------|-----------|------------------|
| 0 | Up | Top horizontal bar |
| 1 | Right | Top-right corner block |
| 2 | Down | Bottom horizontal bar |
| 3 | Left | Top-left corner block |

### Memory Map (Variables)

| Address | Purpose | Notes |
|---------|---------|-------|
| $5B00+ | Variables | Safe for game state |
| $8000+ | Code | Non-contended RAM |
| $4000-$57FF | Screen | Don't use for variables |
| $5800-$5AFF | Attributes | Don't use for variables |

### Instructions Used

| Instruction | Purpose | T-states | Bytes |
|-------------|---------|----------|-------|
| EQU nn | Define label | N/A | 0 |
| LD (nn),A | Store A to memory | 13 | 3 |
| LD A,(nn) | Load memory to A | 13 | 3 |
| CP n | Compare A with value | 7 | 2 |
| CALL nn | Call subroutine | 17 | 3 |
| RET | Return from subroutine | 10 | 1 |

